      "message": "Are we sure that there is no delayed task already scheduled here, which would crash ? It\u0027s not easy to see at least.\n\nGenerally using TimerFd directly seems error-prone because if 2 messages get scheduled it crashes; that makes it hard to migrate existing code that uses Handler too.\n\nI think we\u0027ll need another wrapper class that can handle multiple messages at the time, something like:\n\n```\ninterface ITask {\n    int getTaskType(); // Message.what if wrapping a message\n    long getRunTime(); // as per SystemClock.elapsedRealtime\n    void run(Handler); // Post if a runnable, sendMessage if a Message\n}\nclass MessageTask implements ITask {...}\nclass RunnableTask implements ITask {...}\n\nclass RealtimeScheduler {\n    private final TimerFd mTimer;\n    private final PriorityQueue\u003cITask\u003e mTasks \u003d new PriorityQueue\u003c\u003e(\n        Comparators.comparing(ITask::getRunTime);\n\n    addDelayedTask(ITask);\n    removeTasks(int taskType);\n}\n```",
